                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote8" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 8"><sup>8</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>Mary A. Burke and Anat Bracha, &ldquo;<a href="http://scholar.google.com/scholar_url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.researchgate.net%2Fprofile%2FAnat_Bracha%2Fpublication%2F321228231_How_Big_is_the_Gig%2Flinks%2F5a15b87c4585153b546cadc9%2FHow-Big-is-the-Gig.pdf&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=T&amp;oi=ggp&amp;ct=res&amp;cd=0&amp;d=1637581824798230527&amp;ei=AejCXcD0OoSSmAGLp4u4Bw&amp;scisig=AAGBfm1NNLU7I_uW8w1Xdy47x8YG55lJ0A&amp;nossl=1&amp;ws=1670x773&amp;at=How%20Big%20Is%20the%20Gig%3F">How Big is the Gig</a>?&rdquo; 2018. We note the gig economy is difficult to measure and estimations vary. A recent <a href="https://www.bls.gov/opub/mlr/2018/article/pdf/measuring-labor-market-activity-today.pdf">BLS study</a> compares employment numbers from the CPS with time spent in gainful employment from the American Time Use Survey and found smaller differences than Burke and Bracha.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote9" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 9"><sup>9</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>Based on data prepared by Chmura Economics for the Dan River Region Collaborative.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote10" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 10"><sup>10</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>Statistics on health insurance from the Kaiser Family Foundation, &ldquo;<a href="https://www.kff.org/health-costs/report/2019-employer-health-benefits-survey/">Employer Health Benefits, 2019 Annual Survey</a>.&rdquo;</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote11" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 11"><sup>11</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>Data from JOLTS via Haver Analytics. Turnover rates: retail trade: 5.2 percent; leisure and hospitality (includes accommodation and food services): 6.7 percent; total private industry: 4.2 percent; financial activities: 2.4 percent.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote12" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 12"><sup>12</sup></a>
